  "source_findings": [
    {"id":"A1","finding":"local_embeddedness combines member, pool, formation, and institutional channels as 1-product(1-channel): a substitution/OR architecture."},
    {"id":"A2","finding":"recruitment access uses max of social, formation, member, and foothold access: another strong substitution architecture."},
    {"id":"A3","finding":"action opportunity hazard is proportional to committed fighter equivalents; access/knowledge mostly shape action channel and execution downstream."},
    {"id":"A4","finding":"FootholdState access, target_knowledge, infrastructure, and sustainment are initialized but are not broadly live inputs to foothold dynamics in the audited Rust core; field existence is not mechanism validation."},
    {"id":"A5","finding":"organization adaptation is stochastic phenotype mutation, not clearly reward-directed strategic learning."},
    {"id":"A6","finding":"Phase-E reduced equations are schematic theory, not literal Rust transition equations; reduction must be validated on synthetic trajectories."}
